## Summary

Converted all 16 functions from `KernSmooth/R/all.R` to Python, processed in dependency order (leaves → roots) as required:

1. `.onAttach`, `.onUnload` — no deps
2. `linbin`, `rlbin` — leaf Fortran-binning ports
3. `blkest`, `cpblock`, `linbin2D` — leaf Fortran ports
4. `bkfe`, `locpoly`, `sdiag`, `sstdiag` — depend on `linbin`/`rlbin`
5. `bkde`, `bkde2D`, `dpih`, `dpik` — depend on `linbin`/`linbin2D`/`bkfe`
6. `dpill` — depends on all of `rlbin`, `cpblock`, `blkest`, `locpoly`, `sdiag`, `sstdiag`

All outputs written to `/groups/jli9/Yufei/python-KernSmooth/ablation/conversion_guides/guides/6/all.R/` as JSON files (imports/prototype/body), one per function. One transient rate-limit failure occurred on the first `bkfe` attempt; it was retried successfully per the skill's error-handling policy. Several of the more complex functions (`locpoly`, `bkde`, `bkde2D`) were cross-validated numerically against a live R installation and matched to floating-point precision.
